One day I had a pony I'd tamed with a pear.  I had a big cat so I
didn't care about him, although I wasn't trying to kill him per se.
Anyway, I eventually got a message, "You feel worried about Trigger"
which I guessed meant he was starving (he wasn't in the room at the
time).  Now I had found a wand of polymorph, so when I made some piles
of stuff to change I waited until my poor pony was in the way before
zapping.  He turned into a black dragon!  But a little bit later, I
went back down a corridor where I'd left him and found a black dragon
corpse named Trigger and some scales, and no nasty around.  Question
1: Did his nutrition value carry over when he got polymorphed such
that he starved to death?

Anyway, I knew better than to eat him, but on a whim I tinned him and
ate the tin, and got disintegration resistance without any scolding
from my god.  Later I purposely tinned a corpse I thought was really
old, then ate it without getting food poisoning.  So Question 2: do
tins not keep any information about the corpse they are tinned from,
and if not is what I did an intentional feature or something I
abused?  I certainly felt cheap eating my tinned pet for an intrinsic,
though I don't mind as much getting around food poisoning this way.



